# Design — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

## Code conventions
- Naming, file organisation, and formatting follow the stack's standard tooling (`{{FORMAT}}`).
- One responsibility per module; respect the layer rules in `ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- Prefer explicit over clever; no dead code, no commented-out blocks.

## API patterns (backend)
- Validate every input at the edge; return typed, consistent error shapes.
- Idempotent writes where retries are possible.

## Component patterns (frontend)
- Small composable components; state lives as close to use as possible.

## Logging
- Structured key-value logs (`event=user.login user_id=123 outcome=ok`).
- Never log secrets, tokens, or personal data (see `SECURITY.md`).

## Diagrams
Every flow, sequence, schema, or state diagram is a Mermaid block. Never ASCII art.
